    "datasource": "Fujichrome Provia 400X Professional [RXP], Fujifilm AF3-0213E; SHA256 7bb846970004e5e45151eca08b473010d008aba28c6dc6bbe3e28d8caeee4927. Reproduce with scripts/bw_expansion/prepare_colour_film.py; axis calibration derived from the page by scripts/bw_expansion/extract_graphs.py; source points, assumptions and conditions: data/profile-sources/fuji-provia-400x/recipe.json. Dye spectra: this sheet, with no plotted neutral to rescale against. PCHIP of the three plotted log-sensitivity traces; engine covers 380-780 nm, each trace is used only over its own plotted span and is unmeasured elsewhere. Relative shape only; the panel's E.N.D. density criterion is not an absolute speed. Not on the sheet. The dye panel is normalised to a visual neutral of 1.0 and plots no D-min, and the characteristic panel's minimum is a status-A reading, not a spectral curve. A flat 0.10 is assumed, within the 0.09-0.13 range the shipped positives carry. This is an assumption, not a measurement. Spectral adaptation parameters are not this stock's own: they are borrowed from fujifilm_provia_100f. Nearest shipped sibling: the same manufacturer's E-6 reversal family. Density curves balanced against a rendered 5-stop grey ramp by scripts/bw_expansion/balance_against_ramp.py (upstream's correct_positive_curves_with_gray_ramp): density scale [0.9626, 1.0188, 1.0176], log-exposure shift [-0.054, 0.0, 0.0351], data_trustability 0.5. Worst channel deviation from neutral across the ramp 62.0% before, 3.3% after. This correction is fitted against the engine, not measured from the datasheet."
